<article class="env-proposition" id="03CN">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03CN">Proposition <span data-tag="03CN">7.5.7.1</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a small category and let $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{Kan}$ be a (strictly commutative) diagram of $\infty $-categories indexed by $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then a Kan complex $X$ is a colimit of the functor $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\mathscr {F})$ if and only if it is weakly homotopy equivalent to the homotopy colimit $ \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}(\mathscr {F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\lambda _{t}:  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}(\mathscr {F}) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\mathscr {F}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ be the taut scaffold of Construction <a data-tag="0373" href="/tag/0373">5.3.4.11</a>. Then $\lambda _{t}$ is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets (Corollary <a data-tag="037S" href="/tag/037S">5.3.5.9</a>), and therefore a weak homotopy equivalence (Remark <a data-tag="01EB" href="/tag/01EB">4.5.4.4</a>). The desired result now follows from Corollary <a data-tag="039K" href="/tag/039K">7.4.3.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
